{
  "$comment": "The ONE glyph list of `Inter Symbols`, the key-symbol fallback every eUI renderer puts right after the theme family (`\"Geist\", \"Inter Symbols\", ui-sans-serif, …`), ahead of any OS fallback: Geist and Nunito have no ⌘, so without it each OS substituted its own face and a KbdGroup \"⌘S\" measured differently per platform. `build.py` subsets the desktop's Inter (apps/desktop/assets/fonts, SIL OFL 1.1, no Reserved Font Name) to exactly these codepoints (plus `carried`) at each weight, renames the family, and writes every copy listed in `outputs` (woff2 for the web recipes, ttf for SwiftUI, Compose and gpui); `outputs` records each file's sha256 and `codepointsHash` the list it was built from. `src/web/inter-symbols.test.ts` fails when a copy, a renderer's family name or face list, or the list itself drifts from this file. Rebuild after editing: `uvx --from 'fonttools[woff]==4.69.1' python -I packages/exponential-ui/fonts/build.py`.",
